WEBVTT

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:04.890
Have some fun?

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:06.420
What are you going to do?

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.820
A battle, of course.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:11.940
A battle? But you're—

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:12.880
Suzuko.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:13.570
What?

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:14.990
He's a Selector.

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:19.490
I didn't realize it. Why?

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:22.400
It's my LRIG's special ability.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:26.420
If a fellow Selector were the bookmaker, 
you'd be cautious, right?

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:28.270
And I wouldn't be able to snack on you.

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:29.300
Snack?

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.880
Once the limit approaches,

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:34.070
you have to battle, after all.

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:38.140
When that happens, I pick a random 
loser and secretly beat on them.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.420
Of course, they're not much of a snack...

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.920
Oh, but he was actually quite good!

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:48.190
Shirai-kun, was it?

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.530
His voice was so sweet when he cried!

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.160
The entire time, I felt like I might come!

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:56.820
No, Chi-chan.

00:00:57.940 --> 00:00:59.690
I'll fight him.

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:00.920
Suzu...

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:01.870
Don't worry.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:03.540
I won't lose.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.570
There she goes, the creepy girl.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.940
Seeing her in person makes me want to puke.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:14.670
Isn't that what makes it exciting?

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:17.290
You really are a pervert.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:24.900
Satisfy me, Suzuko-chan.

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:28.030
Open!

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:04.030
Dawn

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:18.010
Suzu...

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:25.890
Riru, grow.

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:31.560
Summon SIGNI Gareth and Percival.

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:33.770
Turn end.

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:36.720
All right, let's do this.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:38.150
Carnival, grow.

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:43.090
Summon SIGNI Ifrid and Antares.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:45.070
Attack!

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:54.880
Turn end.

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:56.000
Suzuko...

00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:57.380
Yeah.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.680
We'll attack and take the initiative.

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:01.880
Riru, grow.

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:03.920
Coin bet!

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.010
Honest!

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:12.690
Show me every card in your hand.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.600
Sure thing.

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:18.220
We can handle that.

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:18.670
Yeah.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:21.320
Deploy SIGNI, and full attack.

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:26.330
Turn end!

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:28.660
Way to go, Suzuko-chan.

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:31.460
I can tell you've made it this far

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:35.920
by crushing many Selectors underfoot 
and stealing their treasured memories.

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:38.540
You thought it felt good, right?

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:43.510
When they screamed and cried 
as you finished them!

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:44.690
That's not—

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:46.140
It's all right!

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:49.840
The strong have the right to devour the weak.

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:51.050
Why?

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:52.390
We're both Selectors.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:56.650
You should know how scary battles are 
and how painful it is to lose your memories!

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:57.430
So why?!

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:58.660
Who knows?

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:00.110
Carnival, grow.

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:03.320
Coin bet.

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:06.640
Joker.

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:09.620
Change Antares to Machupi.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.410
The card changed?

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:14.500
That's his power?

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.500
Banish all SIGNI!

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:20.130
<i>No...</i>

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.600
Full attack!

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:27.970
Riru!

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:30.930
My power is Joker.

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:34.220
I can do this, too.

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:35.910
Coin bet.

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:38.690
Berserk.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:49.170
No!

00:05:49.170 --> 00:05:50.000
Suzuko...

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:52.080
Riru, grow.

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:56.250
You know it's useless, right?

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:58.350
Coin...

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:02.000
bet...

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.020
Honest!

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:04.800
Use Honest...

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:06.360
on me.

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:08.550
What is she doing?

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:17.730
Berserk...

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:22.440
She dispelled it with her 
own desire to not attack?

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:26.030
So this is how Suzu fights?

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.100
I love it... I love it!

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:33.970
Suzuko-chan, excite me even more.

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:36.410
Battles have to feel good!

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:41.380
It reminds me of when I was an LRIG.

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:43.420
He was an LRIG?

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:46.260
The battles were so fun...

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:49.680
The way we sliced each other's lives apart.

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:53.510
Looking down on my opponent's 
despairing faces, mocking them.

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:55.740
But...

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:57.680
I quickly got bored.

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:03.240
Everyone kept clinging to 
their garbage memories,

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:04.860
driving themselves to destruction.

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:08.290
There's nothing wrong with crushing weak bugs,

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:10.540
but it just didn't make me feel good.

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:15.260
Eventually, the Selector I was 
paired with disappeared, too.

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:17.660
I tried living in his body,

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:20.540
but what I really craved...

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:26.420
were those battles in the rift 
between life and death!

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:30.880
That is an LRIG's instinct.

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:31.880
Right?

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:37.180
And so, I had the greatest idea imaginable.

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:39.580
I would be a Selector myself

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:43.380
and control all of the battles!

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:47.560
And the card chose me, just as I wanted.

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:49.820
And an LRIG came to me.

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:54.070
Carnival was my ideal LRIG!

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:59.860
I leaked information about the bookmaker, 
and those fools all rushed to me.

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:04.370
I was having fun making them kill 
each other in their despair,

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:07.840
when I came up with an even better idea!

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:10.960
I'd find the strongest creature,

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:14.280
one unbound by garbage memories,

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:16.720
raise them up, and destroy them!

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:19.040
The most enjoyable game imaginable!

00:08:19.710 --> 00:08:20.530
You're wrong.

00:08:21.570 --> 00:08:22.770
Memories...

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:26.170
Memories aren't garbage.

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:30.320
It's because of my memories that 
I'm standing here right now!

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:35.380
Then just try and use that 
sentiment to kill me.

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:36.610
Grow.

00:08:36.610 --> 00:08:39.150
Summon Gaiten, Regulus.

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:41.000
Attack!

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:45.020
Carnival, attack!

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:47.380
Guard with Servant!

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:48.710
Coin bet.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:52.050
Joker!

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:54.880
Delete the servant's abilities on her card!

00:09:03.030 --> 00:09:05.440
She can even change her opponent's cards?

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:06.900
Hey, Riru...

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:10.470
We were born to battle.

00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:12.290
Humans, this world...

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:15.380
They're all tools for enjoying the battle!

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:17.160
That's what an LRIG is.

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:19.400
Isn't it?

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:22.160
Come on, join me.

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:25.440
Once the ninety days are over,

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:27.830
your battle as an LRIG is over.

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:32.820
But if you become human, you can be 
a Selector as many times as you want

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:35.410
and keep fighting the battles.

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:36.830
It's simple!

00:09:36.830 --> 00:09:38.880
Just lose the battle!

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:41.790
Then Suzuko-chan's body will be yours!

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:42.640
What are you—

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:44.100
Now, come with me, Riru.

00:09:44.420 --> 00:09:46.440
Let's have fun

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:48.930
with this piece-of-shit world!

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:55.190
Riru?

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:02.330
That sounds pretty good.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:06.570
Riru?

00:10:08.970 --> 00:10:10.250
It's your turn.

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:12.790
Riru, grow.

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:17.760
Riru, attack!

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:23.550
Riru? Why?

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:26.010
Because I'm an LRIG.

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:30.100
Like I just told you,

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:32.190
that's an LRIG's instinct.

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:36.320
Riru, you're joking, right?

00:10:37.140 --> 00:10:39.740
If that's what you think, then find out.

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:41.110
Find out?

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:44.790
Coin bet!

00:10:47.390 --> 00:10:48.080
Honest.

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:50.060
Use Honest on Riru.

00:10:54.910 --> 00:10:57.460
Riru, tell me how you really feel.

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:02.070
I battle for what I believe in.

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:03.470
That's all.

00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:05.510
What you believe in?

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:07.930
Turn end.

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:11.090
You were betrayed by Riru, whom you trusted.

00:11:11.090 --> 00:11:14.110
The despair is about to drive you mad, isn't it?

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:16.420
This is crazy!

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:17.320
It's so exciting...

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:21.050
I think I'm gonna have the best climax ever.

00:11:21.050 --> 00:11:23.330
Carnival, grow.

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:27.950
Hey, it's not fair to keep all 
the pleasure for yourself.

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:30.160
Okay, go finish her.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:32.260
Carnival, attack!

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:37.550
Activate ARTS, Kill Two Birds with One Stone.

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:40.260
Stop their attack, and deal damage!

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:45.050
What?

00:11:45.230 --> 00:11:45.840
Too slow!

00:11:51.990 --> 00:11:53.690
Riru was pretending to betray her?

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:57.460
She caused them to delay the coin bet

00:11:57.460 --> 00:12:00.380
so they couldn't use Joker to nullify the attack.

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:01.750
Suzuko...

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:05.600
I envy how much they trust each other.

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:06.620
Meru...

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:07.920
I believed in you.

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:08.580
Me, too.

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:17.960
So you're saying this bitch girl 
and her bitch LRIG tricked me?

00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:23.050
Too bad, you stupid former LRIG.

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:27.700
Wonderful.

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:30.530
Your hope, your trust,

00:12:30.530 --> 00:12:32.610
what you want to protect...

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:35.480
I'll destroy it all!

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:37.230
<b>The Hidden Mystery of WIXOSS... 
It began with a girl named Mayu.</b>

00:12:44.020 --> 00:12:45.120
Understanding.

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:46.670
Shirai-san is gone.

00:12:46.670 --> 00:12:47.990
I regret it.

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:53.040
Perhaps I made things harder for Suzuko-chan...

00:12:54.340 --> 00:12:55.320
Unnecessary.

00:12:55.320 --> 00:12:56.740
You don't need to worry.

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:00.840
Suzuko-san is strong.

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:03.010
Riru, attack.

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:06.050
Banish Saizou with spell 
Victory Song of Chain Destruction!

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:08.010
Banish effect, Rise Search!

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:10.850
Send Annabelle to the trash to play Impact!

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:12.530
Life Burst!

00:13:12.530 --> 00:13:13.810
Banish Tendou!

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:24.710
They're both running low on Life Cloth.

00:13:25.290 --> 00:13:27.240
They each have one coin left.

00:13:28.650 --> 00:13:30.070
Coin bet.

00:13:31.590 --> 00:13:32.580
Blind.

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:36.370
Turn end.

00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:37.840
They can even use blind?

00:13:37.840 --> 00:13:39.940
Suzuko, it's our turn.

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:40.640
Right.

00:13:40.640 --> 00:13:42.030
Coin bet!

00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:44.380
Honest!

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:51.120
Tell me specifically where all the cards 
hidden by Blind are, as well as their types.

00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:52.460
Bravo!

00:13:52.460 --> 00:13:55.020
That was the perfect way to ask that question!

00:13:55.820 --> 00:13:57.420
Will this do?

00:13:58.610 --> 00:13:59.590
No traps.

00:13:59.590 --> 00:14:00.190
Yeah.

00:14:00.390 --> 00:14:02.070
Summon SIGNI!

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:03.550
Full attack!

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:09.620
He has one Life Cloth left.

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:12.160
Satomi used his final coin.

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:14.660
He can't change his cards with Joker anymore.

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:15.910
In other words...

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:19.210
Looks like this is my final turn.

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:21.790
ARTS Phosphorescent Samsara.

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:24.630
Let's go big.

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:25.420
She's coming.

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:26.280
Yeah.

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:29.430
If we counter with ARTS 
Deluge of Water Currents—

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:29.860
What?

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:31.860
Our Multi Ener...

00:14:32.710 --> 00:14:34.890
Did he do that back then?

00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:39.340
Looks like you can't pay 
enough to use that card!

00:14:39.340 --> 00:14:40.850
Too bad!

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:42.350
That was his goal?

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:44.780
It was fun, Suzuko-chan...

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:46.650
It really was.

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:49.610
I'm so glad you've grown up this much.

00:14:49.610 --> 00:14:51.820
Let me see your face.

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:52.820
Don't worry.

00:14:52.820 --> 00:14:55.160
I'll always remember you.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:57.790
You'll be a beloved memory of mine.

00:14:57.790 --> 00:14:59.860
Now, it's time for the finale.

00:14:59.860 --> 00:15:01.500
End it, Carnival.

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:05.340
You're sure you want me 
to crush your toy, Kou?

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:06.840
Suzu...

00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:08.300
Meru!

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:12.110
Can you bet my coin on Suzu?

00:15:12.110 --> 00:15:13.290
I don't know.

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:14.900
But are you serious?

00:15:14.900 --> 00:15:15.620
Yes.

00:15:17.420 --> 00:15:18.060
I won't.

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:19.320
Meru!

00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:21.770
Because if Suzu disappears, you'll—

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:24.030
This is our battle, too!

00:15:24.930 --> 00:15:27.250
Fight with me, Meru.

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:29.990
Together?

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:32.910
That's the first time you've said that.

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:36.530
Thank you, Meru.

00:15:36.770 --> 00:15:37.580
Suzu!

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:39.540
Chi-chan?

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:41.060
Use this!

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:45.440
You can do it.

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:48.670
Right.

00:15:49.520 --> 00:15:50.740
Coin bet!

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:54.300
Requiem.

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:57.180
Wh-What?

00:15:57.710 --> 00:15:59.040
What's going to happen?

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:00.340
I don't know.

00:16:00.340 --> 00:16:04.740
But I think it's fusing the power 
of Berserk and Honest,

00:16:04.740 --> 00:16:07.100
turning the Selector's true wish,

00:16:07.100 --> 00:16:10.360
the strength of her heart, into attack power!

00:16:11.260 --> 00:16:13.460
What are you doing?

00:16:13.460 --> 00:16:14.450
Don't spoil the mood!

00:16:15.060 --> 00:16:16.660
You useless idiot!

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:26.170
Just...

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:31.670
die already!

00:16:33.710 --> 00:16:35.180
<i>Riru won't lose.</i>

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:36.760
<i>We won't lose.</i>

00:16:37.560 --> 00:16:39.070
<i>If the two of us are together!</i>

00:16:50.550 --> 00:16:51.990
It won't end.

00:16:53.590 --> 00:16:55.570
The darkness won't end.

00:16:56.130 --> 00:17:00.320
As long as there are disgusting 
creatures that are no more

00:17:00.320 --> 00:17:03.040
than bags stuffed with memories and greed,

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:05.500
the battles will begin again.

00:17:06.070 --> 00:17:10.220
They'll struggle, suffer, scream, despair...

00:17:10.220 --> 00:17:13.160
And I will watch them and laugh.

00:17:24.800 --> 00:17:26.080
We won.

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:26.900
Yeah.

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:29.690
I heard your voice.

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:30.670
Riru, I—

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:31.690
Thank you.

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:35.660
I became who I am now because of you.

00:17:35.660 --> 00:17:36.610
Riru...

00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:40.300
Your earnest emotions changed me.

00:17:41.170 --> 00:17:42.080
I...

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:44.950
Because you were always with me, I...

00:17:46.110 --> 00:17:47.170
That's why...

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:49.630
Take good care of Chinatsu.

00:17:50.700 --> 00:17:53.090
You searched with all your heart for Chinatsu.

00:17:53.440 --> 00:17:55.140
It was almost saddening to see.

00:17:55.980 --> 00:17:56.930
Riru!

00:17:57.920 --> 00:18:01.460
Finally, do you have any wishes 
for your memories?

00:18:02.150 --> 00:18:03.390
I want to remember you.

00:18:05.140 --> 00:18:07.270
I never want to forget you.

00:18:16.300 --> 00:18:17.950
I'll never forget.

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:22.200
I won't forget, either.

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:23.410
Yeah.

00:18:28.270 --> 00:18:29.220
Riru...

00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:31.170
Suzu.

00:18:33.260 --> 00:18:34.350
Welcome back.

00:18:36.540 --> 00:18:42.100
Chi-chan, Riru... Riru is gone!

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:44.890
I'm so tired of all this!

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:49.060
I won't fight any more battles.

00:18:49.910 --> 00:18:53.020
I'll treasure the memories you protected.

00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:56.480
I won't run anymore.

00:18:57.070 --> 00:19:00.200
Even if something painful happens, 
I'll just focus on the future.

00:19:01.230 --> 00:19:02.580
Just like you, Suzu.

00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:07.120
Yeah.

00:19:15.020 --> 00:19:16.170
Sorry.

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:17.790
Welcome back, Dad.

00:19:18.380 --> 00:19:19.340
Did you wait long?

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:20.970
A little, yeah.

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:25.200
He's home.

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:26.810
I'm back.

00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:27.880
Welcome back.

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:28.810
Welcome home.

00:19:29.570 --> 00:19:31.080
This is quite a feast today.

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:32.860
I made it.

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:39.630
Hey, is the candy store we always went to 
in elementary school still there?

00:19:39.630 --> 00:19:40.860
Yeah, it is.

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:42.780
We used to go there all the time.

00:19:42.780 --> 00:19:44.620
They had gummies, chocolate, ice cream...

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:48.540
We'd agree to spend up to 100 yen,
then eat our snacks in the park.

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:50.000
Then we did our homework.

00:19:50.480 --> 00:19:53.980
I'm sorry you always had to tutor me.

00:19:53.980 --> 00:19:56.100
You were better at Japanese.

00:19:56.100 --> 00:19:58.000
That was all!

00:20:00.440 --> 00:20:02.610
We had fun again today, huh?

00:20:02.610 --> 00:20:03.550
Yeah.

00:20:03.920 --> 00:20:05.750
Okay, I'll see you tomorrow.

00:20:05.750 --> 00:20:07.540
Yeah, see you tomorrow.

00:20:17.450 --> 00:20:19.480
Chi-chan, it's time.

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:22.450
It is.

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:33.030
So this is farewell.

00:20:34.260 --> 00:20:34.940
Yes.

00:20:37.190 --> 00:20:38.750
Hey, Chi-chan...

00:20:39.090 --> 00:20:41.550
Am I like Suzu?

00:20:42.560 --> 00:20:45.160
I was always too scared to ask.

00:20:45.160 --> 00:20:47.060
Because I'm an LRIG,

00:20:47.820 --> 00:20:49.700
and all I can do is fight.

00:20:50.320 --> 00:20:52.780
I can't be Suzu...

00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:54.190
No.

00:20:54.980 --> 00:20:56.220
You're you.

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:58.770
No one else.

00:21:00.140 --> 00:21:03.190
Thank you for always being by my side.

00:21:03.930 --> 00:21:05.910
You're a dear friend, Meru.

00:21:07.720 --> 00:21:08.490
Chi-chan...

00:21:18.740 --> 00:21:19.880
Thank you.

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:22.130
It was fun, Chi-chan.

00:21:22.600 --> 00:21:23.300
Yeah.

00:21:27.960 --> 00:21:31.410
Chi-chan, no matter what 
happens, we're always...

00:21:31.930 --> 00:21:32.440
Yeah.

00:21:33.360 --> 00:21:36.140
Friends forever.

00:22:15.450 --> 00:22:16.770
Hello!

00:22:31.480 --> 00:22:33.420
This kind of feels nice, huh?

00:22:33.420 --> 00:22:34.350
Um...

00:22:35.190 --> 00:22:36.090
Are you—

00:22:36.090 --> 00:22:37.810
That's cute!

00:22:39.320 --> 00:22:41.500
I've had it since I was a child.

00:22:42.160 --> 00:22:44.710
I don't remember why...

00:22:45.440 --> 00:22:47.990
But it's important.

00:22:49.430 --> 00:22:51.210
Very important.

00:22:55.160 --> 00:22:57.280
I'm Homura Suzuko!

00:22:57.280 --> 00:22:58.270
Who are you?

00:23:00.640 --> 00:23:04.260
Chinatsu... Morikawa Chinatsu.

00:23:04.260 --> 00:23:06.060
Chi-chan, then!

00:23:06.680 --> 00:23:08.950
Let's be friends, Chi-chan.

00:23:24.050 --> 00:23:25.760
<i>Someday, I'm sure...</i>

00:23:26.520 --> 00:23:28.080
<i>It'll be like that day.</i>

00:23:31.180 --> 00:23:32.610
<i>If the two of us are together,</i>

00:23:33.380 --> 00:23:36.370
<i>I'm sure... Someday...</i>
